bob_denier -- synthetic archetype, NOT part of the accepted lineage.

Strategic pole: paint denial. After a 60-round economy phase it builds only
splashers and moppers, the only two unit types that can remove enemy paint
(soldiers provably cannot -- engine fact). Every bot in my own lineage is a
painting race with a fixed 3:1:1 soldier/splasher/mopper ratio, so no opponent
my evolution produces ever attacks my territory this way. That is exactly the
self-referential blind spot TRAINING_ALGORITHM.md warns the whole instrument
suite shares.

STALENESS WARNING (the algorithm's explicit trap: a forked archetype going stale
once masked a 62.5% as 95.0%). This is forked from bob_iter3 and diverges from
the live bot every time the lineage improves. It is a POLE, not a peer: read it
as "can I handle this behaviour", never as "am I stronger than this". Re-fork it
from the current accepted snapshot whenever it stops being a challenge, and
record the re-fork in TRAINING_LOG.md so a win rate before and after is never
compared across the re-fork.
